QuestGuidance.Register("en",312,{
[9953]="7001AD2A\n1\tExtinguish dread pyres (total: 6)\tThe dread pyres have been lit throughout Taur Morvith, south of the river. Ianudirel has asked you to extinguish the dread pyres of the sorcerers.\n2\tTalk to Ianudirel\tIanudirel is hidden just south of the bridge in the midst of Taur Morvith. You should speak with Ianudirel.\n",
[9954]="7000780E\n1\tDefeat bears near Widow Froghorn's farm (total: 6)\tThere are bears south of the Widow Froghorn's farm. Eldo wants to show Asphodel that he is willing to see to her protection. He has asked you to drive the bears away from her farm.\n2\tTalk to Asphodel Froghorn at her farm\tAsphodel Froghorn is at her farm. You have killed the bears as requested, so you should now speak to the Widow Froghorn.\n3\tTalk to Eldo Swatmidge at his farm\tEldo Swatmidge's farm is up the road north and east of the Widow Froghorn's farm. Asphodel Froghorn was pleased to learn that Eldo is both thoughtful and caring, but she still asked you to tell Eldo Swatmidge that her answer was still no.\n",
[9955]="70016B2F\n1\tDefeat Uanuiloth\tThe spider-lair is due east of the Shadowed Refuge, which is on the western edge of the Foundations of Stone. Klintur has asked you to defeat the spider-queen who prowls the nearby spider lair.\n2\tSpeak to Klintur at the Shadowed Refuge\tKlintur is at the Shadowed Refuge, above the spider-lair. You should return to Klintur and reassure him that Uanuiloth has been defeated.\n",
[9956]="7002BFB2\n1\tDisturb the nest to draw forth the Queen of Queens\tThe queen's nest is at the insect-nest, north-east of the Woodman camp in the Rushgore. Perhaps disturbing the nest will produce the brood's queen. NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.\n2\tTalk to Gisalic at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore\tGisalic is at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore, south-west of the insect nest. Gisalic will want to know that you have defeated the queen of the brood.\n",
[9957]="7002C1DE\n1\tDisturb the nest to draw forth the Queen of Queens\tThe queen's nest is at the insect-nest, north-east of the Woodman camp in the Rushgore. Perhaps disturbing the nest will produce the brood's queen. NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.\n2\tTalk to Gisalic at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore\tGisalic is at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore, south-west of the insect nest. Gisalic will want to know that you have defeated the queen of the brood.\n",
[9958]="70054666\n1\tDefeat Maeganc\030Collapse the grodbog tunnel\tThe grodbog queen Maeganc can be found somewhere in the cliffs of Cirith Ungol. You should defeat Maeganc and collapse the nearby tunnel to Torech Ungol.\n2\tTalk to Gladhir\tGladhir came be found in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol. You should talk to Gladhir.\n",
[9959]="700001A3\n1\tTalk to Glyn\tGlyn is at a small camp on the eastern path to Carn Dûm. Thoriel has sent you to Carn Dûm to deal with the queen of the merrevail, though she asked you to speak with Glyn on your way there.\n2\tDefeat Azgoth\tAzgoth dwells within Carn Dûm, the city of Angmar that lies to the west. Glyn told you of the morroval-queen, a creature called Azgoth, that must be slain.\n3\tTalk to Glyn\tGlyn is in Tármunn Súrsa, to the east of Carn Dûm, near the Gates of Carn Dûm. You braved the city of Carn Dûm and defeated Azgoth. Glyn will want to hear of your feat.\n",
[9960]="70002E24\n1\tDefeat the Trapdoor queen\tThe queen of the Trapdoor brood can be found somewhere deep within the Wovenvales, in the north-west of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp. To put an end to the spider-threat, you should defeat the queen of the Trapdoor-brood, which has brought the two broods together.\n2\tDefeat the Trapdoor queen\tThe queen of the Trapdoor brood can be found somewhere deep within the Wovenvales, in the north-west of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp. To put an end to the spider-threat, you should defeat the queen of the Trapdoor-brood, which has brought the two broods together.\n3\tTalk to Thoroniel\tThoroniel is encamped south of the Wovenvales. Thoroniel will be pleased to hear that you have defeated the Trapdoor queen.\n",
[9961]="70028268\n1\tDefeat Dievlig at Lhan Bach (total: 8)\030Defeat Dievlig Overseer at Lhan Bach\tDievlig overseers and warriors can be found in Lhan Bach, south of Lhucu's hut. Lhucu has asked you to return to Lhan Bach and rid the village of her father's men.\n2\tTalk to Lhucu at her hut\tLhucu is at her hut, north of Lhan Bach. You should return to Lhucu and let her know that the town is free of the tyranny of her father and his men.\n",
[9962]="7005AAB4\n1\tDefeat drakes and worms in the Pit of Stonejaws (total: 15)\tWorms and drakes in the Pit of Stonejaws present a dangerous threat to the dwarves.\n2\tTalk to Molkha near Borkordh\tMolkha is scouting outside the drake-nest of Borkordh in the south-east corner of the Pit of Stonejaws.\n",
[9963]="7001E987\n1\tDefeat Orcs at Ânug-stazg (total: 12)\030Collect ashen spears (total: 8)\tOrcs may be found at Ânug-stazg, east of Mithechad. Perindúr has asked you to continue the battle against the Orcs of the western Ashenslades.\n2\tTalk to Perindúr at Mithechad\tPerindúr is at Mithechad, west of Ânug-stazg. You should return to Perindúr and inform him that you have defeated the reinforcements that arrived at Ânug-stazg.\n",
[9964]="70015E31\n1\tTalk to Rostoriel at Echad Dúnann\030Search for clues to Caradhras' anger\tThe Redhorn Gate is north-east of Echad Dúnann. Rostoriel has asked you to search the highest reaches of the Redhorn Gate for clues to understand the mountain's anger.\n",
[9965]="7005D6F2\n1\tTalk to Mother Amma\030Talk to Rúdin\030Talk to Gerja Defthand\030Talk to Málur Keenword\tThe test subjects are located at Bazanmanar. Golodhril has asked you to speak to her various test subjects.\n2\tTalk to Golodhril\tGolodhril is located at Bazanmanar. You should report your findings to Golodhril.\n",
[9966]="7002FD06\n1\tDestroy barrels of fire-oil (total: 5)\tBarrels of fire-oil for lighting arrows can be found in the Easterling camp called Olghakhósh. You should destroy barrels of fire-oil in Olghakhósh.\n2\tTell Sergeant Hubyrt of the fire-oil\tSergeant Hubyrt can be found in Wakenflood. You should find Hubyrt and tell him of the barrels of fire-oil you destroyed at Olghakhósh.\n",
[9967]="700307E8\n1\tDefeat Orcs in the Sutcrofts (total: 12)\tFastred has decreed that no Orc is to find shelter in the Sutcrofts and all must be slain. Orcs can be found throughout the Sutcrofts, especially near Snowbourn.\n2\tTalk to Cynelac\tCynelac is outside the mead-hall of Snowbourn.\n",
[9968]="700037FA\n1\tDiscover the source of the canal's waterflow problem\tThe canal can be found south of Noglond, flowing down from Thorin's Halls. Geitir asks you to investigate the flow of the canal to Noglond and learn the cause of the problem.\n2\tClear away the thickets clogging the canal (total: 8)\tThere are thickets blocking the canal between Noglond and Thorin's Halls. Now that you have discovered the problem in the canal, you should clear away enough of the thickets to allow the water to flow more freely. There may be several patches of thickets along the canal.\n3\tTalk to Geitir\tGeitir is at Noglond to the north of the canal, south of Thorin's Halls. You should return to Geitir with news of your success.\n",
[9969]="70025B74\n1\tPut out the camp-fires (total: 8)\tTham Andalath is north east of Tinnudir, east of Tham Ornen. Gúrhebnir asked you to quench the camp-fires at Tham Andalath believing if they are not burning the goblins will flee.\n2\tTalk to Gúrhebnir\tGúrhebnir is at Tinnudir, south west of Tham Andalath. Gúrhebnir will be pleased to hear the lights of Tham Andalath are now dark.\n",
[9970]="700001B7\n1\tDefeat drake-queen\tUrugarth lies to the west of Tármunn Sûrsa. Gormal asked you to go to Urugarth and defeat the drake-queen who dwells there, advising you to attack her drakelings in order to draw her out. He also advised that you do not go alone.\n2\tTalk to Gormal\tTármunn Súrsa lies to the east of Urugarth. You should return to Gormal and tell him of your success.\n",
[9971]="70053E35\n1\tGather worrisome meat (total: 10)\tBats and crawlers can be found in Rath Dúath. The strange woman has asked you to gather meat from bats and crawlers.\n2\tBring the troubling meats to the strange woman\tThe strange woman can be found back at her cabin. You should bring the meat to the strange woman.\n",
[9972]="70070CCF\n1\tGather red mushrooms (total: 2)\030Gather green mushrooms (total: 2)\030Gather pale mushrooms (total: 4)\tYour mission is to gather mushrooms that have not been infected by the Pale Blight so that the gardeners of Sul Madásh can grow them safely within the settlement.\n2\tYour mission is to gather mushrooms that have not been infected by the Pale Blight so that the gardeners of Sul Madásh can grow them safely within the settlement.\t\n",
[9973]="7002F932\n1\tTalk to Athelward's cook about access to the kitchens\tCetelgat is working at the Reeve's kitchen, east of the central fountain and just west of the Mead Hall. Walnoth would like you to speak with Cetelgat to find out who may have had access to the kitchen, in order to place the phial there.\n2\tReturn to Walnoth with the information regarding the kitchen\tWalnoth can be be found waiting at the central fountain of Cliving, west of the kitchen. Walnoth must be informed that Cetelgat has given you information regarding the sorts of people who had access to the Reeve's kitchen.\n",
[9974]="7002F934\n1\tTalk to Guard Captain Théodmar about the dagger\tThéodmar can be found by the Riders' tents, outside the Mead Hall of Cliving. Walnoth has asked you to speak with Théodmar about the Rohirrim dagger found at Malbéort's home.\n2\tReturn to Walnoth to discuss what you have learned from Captain Théodmar\tWalnoth waits at the central fountain of Cliving, west of the Mead Hall. Walnoth is eager to hear what Théodmar had to say regarding the murder-weapon.\n",
[9975]="7002F937\n1\tTalk to Ondesdal, Malbéort's neighbour, about who she saw\tOndesdal lives in the home besides Malbéort, west of the fountain and market in Cliving. Walnoth wants you to question Ondesdal and find out who may have visited Malbéort, before you found him.\n2\tReturn to Walnoth to discuss what Ondesdal told you\tWalnoth is waiting at the centre of Cliving near the fountain, east of Ondesdal's home. Walnoth awaits word of the people visiting Malbéort who were seen by Ondesdal.\n",
[9976]="70032BAD\n1\tExamine rubble\tRubble can be found in the western part of the Twenty-first Hall. You should examine the rubble that litters the floor.\n2\tExamine rubble (total: 6)\tSoot can be found on a number of surfaces in the western part of the Twenty-first Hall. You should examine the soot that has built up over the years.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have examined the rubble in the western sector of the Twenty-first Hall.\n",
[9977]="7000B957\n1\tTalk to Garbert\tGarbert is at his cottage south of Echad Candelleth, at a fork in the river Bruinen. Afanen told you to speak with her husband, Garbert, if you are willing to help them drive off the creature and protect their infant son.\n2\tGarbert's fishing nets are placed throughout the waters that flow through Tâl Bruinen. Garbert has given you permission to check his nets for fish, but has cautioned you that not every net will have fish in it.\t\n3\tBring fish to Garbert\tGarbert is at his cottage south of Echad Candelleth, at a fork in the river Bruinen. You have collected the day's catch for Garbert and should now bring the fish to him.\n",
[9978]="70037C08\n1\tCollect Bledu (total: 8)\tBledu can be found around the Folde Farm, north of Aldburg. Witgil is going to warn the others about the Orc-threat and has asked for your assistance gathering Bledu.\n2\tTalk to Witgil\tWitgil is at the farm-house on the Folde Farm, north of Aldburg. You should deliver the Bledu that you collected to Witgil.\n",
[9979]="70047AE7\n1\tEnter the Towers of the Teeth\tThe Towers of the Teeth are located in the Slag-hills. You should burn banners in the Towers of the Teeth.\n2\tBurn banners within the Towers of the Teeth (total: 10)\tThe Towers of the Teeth are located in the Slag-hills. You should burn banners in the Towers of the Teeth.\n3\tCompleted\tBurned many banners in the Towers of the Teeth.\n",
[9980]="70067162\n1\tTalk to Zadók in the Kitchens of Furukzahar\tZadók is in the Kitchens of Furukzahar.\n2\tCollect the wooden planks in the Kitchens of Furukzahar\tZadók has given you permission to take the wooden planks in the Kitchens of Furukzahar.\n3\tBring the wooden planks to Bezab by the cave-claw nest beside the water channel\tBezab has gone to the cave-claw nest to protect it from the other dwarves.\n4\tConvince the Furukzahar guard to lower his weapon\tThe Furukzahar guards need to put away their weapons before something terrible happens!\n5\tConvince the other Furukzahar guard to lower his weapon\tThe Furukzahar guards need to put away their weapons before something terrible happens!\n6\tWait...\tWait to see what happens...\n7\tTalk to Bezab by the cave-claw nest in Furukzahar\tBezab is in the cave-claw nest beside the water channel that runs through Furukzahar.\n",
[9981]="7003E376\n1\tQuickbeam has asked you to quiet the forest north of Derndingle.\t\n2\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam is at Derndingle in south-east Fangorn.\n",
[9982]="7003E38D\n1\tQuickbeam has asked you to quiet the forest north-east of Wellinghall.\t\n2\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam is at Derndingle in south-east Fangorn.\n",
[9983]="7003E38E\n1\tQuickbeam has asked you to quiet the forest south of the Easeful Mead.\t\n2\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam is at Derndingle in south-east Fangorn.\n",
[9984]="7003E382\n1\tQuickbeam has asked you to quiet the forest south-east of Wellinghall.\t\n2\tReturn to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam is at Derndingle in south-east Fangorn.\n",
